  "problem": "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\nx{y}^{\u2033}+4y{y}^{\u2032}-3y=3{x}^{2},\\,y(1)=1,\\,{y}^{\u2032}(1)=0\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method by introducing $z={y}^{\u2032}$ and reducing the equation to a system of first-order ODEs. What entries should be placed in the columns for $\u0394y$ and $\u0394z$ in the table below if the step size is $\u0394x=\\frac{1}{2}?$\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{\u2032}$ | $\u0394y$ | $z$ | ${z}^{\u2032}$ | $\u0394z$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ |  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  | {{field-2}} |\n\nTherefore, $y(\\frac{3}{2})\u2248$\n{{field-3}}.",
